      "page_title": "Docker Compose",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What Compose Does",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One ==compose.yaml== defines a multi-container app",
            "`docker compose up` creates and starts every service",
            "Top-level keys: services, networks, volumes, configs, secrets",
            "Compose v2 is the `docker compose` plugin; v1 is retired"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Service Fields",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Field",
            "Purpose",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`image` / `build`",
              "Source of the image",
              "`build: .`"
            ],
            [
              "`ports`",
              "Publish to host",
              "`\"8080:80\"`"
            ],
            [
              "`environment`",
              "Set variables",
              "`DB_HOST=db`"
            ],
            [
              "`volumes`",
              "Persist or mount",
              "`data:/var/lib`"
            ],
            [
              "`restart`",
              "Self-healing",
              "`unless-stopped`"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. A Small Stack",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "services:",
            "  web:",
            "    build: .",
            "    ports: [\"8080:80\"]",
            "    depends_on:",
            "      db: {condition: service_healthy}"
          ],
          "note": "web reaches the db at host db"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Networking and Readiness",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Compose makes a default project network automatically",
            "Services reach each other by ==service name==, not IP",
            "`depends_on` controls start order only, not readiness",
            "Add `healthcheck` plus `condition: service_healthy` to wait",
            "`healthcheck` takes test, interval, timeout, retries, start_period"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4b. Config and Overrides",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`${VAR:-default}` substitution reads values from a `.env` file",
            "`env_file` loads variables into the container",
            "`compose.override.yaml` merges automatically; use `-f` to layer prod",
            "**Profiles** start optional services such as debug tools or seed jobs"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Daily Commands",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`up -d` runs detached; `down` removes; `down -v` drops volumes",
            "`logs -f` tails output; `ps` lists; `exec web sh` opens a shell",
            "`build` rebuilds images; `config` renders the final merged file",
            "`docker compose watch` syncs or rebuilds on file change: fast dev loop"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`down -v` deletes named volumes and your **database data**",
            "Assuming `depends_on` waits until the database is ready",
            "Connecting by container IP instead of the service name"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Key Takeaways",
          "text": "One compose.yaml, service-name DNS, healthchecks for readiness, and never `down -v` on data."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Multi-container apps"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Registries and Image Distribution",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What a Registry Is",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A ==registry== stores and serves images by repo and tag",
            "{icon:docker} Docker Hub, {icon:github} GHCR, {icon:ecr} ECR, GCR/Artifact Registry, ACR",
            "Self-hosted options: Harbor or the `registry:2` image",
            "Address: `ghcr.io/acme/api:1.4.2`"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Push Flow and Layers",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "docker login",
                "sub": "credentials"
              },
              {
                "text": "docker tag",
                "sub": "name the image"
              },
              {
                "text": "docker push",
                "sub": "send"
              },
              {
                "text": "Skip known layers",
                "sub": "already remote"
              },
              {
                "text": "Upload new layers",
                "sub": "only the delta"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Only layers **missing** remotely are uploaded",
            "Layers are content-addressed by `sha256` digest",
            "Identical layers are stored and pulled ==once==",
            "A shared base image costs one copy per registry"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Manifests and Tag Strategy",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A ==manifest== lists layer digests plus the config",
            "A manifest list (index) picks the image per **architecture**",
            "Use immutable version tags and git SHA tags",
            "Keep a moving `latest` only for convenience"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Reference",
            "Mutable?",
            "Use for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`:1.4.2`",
              "No (by policy)",
              "Releases"
            ],
            [
              "`:3f9c2ab`",
              "No",
              "Git traceability"
            ],
            [
              "`:latest`",
              "Yes, moves",
              "Quick local pulls"
            ],
            [
              "`@sha256:…`",
              "Never",
              "Exact deploys"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Multi-Arch Build and Push",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker buildx build \\",
            "  --platform \\",
            "  linux/amd64,linux/arm64 \\",
            "  -t ghcr.io/acme/api:1.4.2 \\",
            "  --push ."
          ],
          "note": "--push uploads the index and both images"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Access, Limits and Cost",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Pin deployments by digest for exact reproducibility",
            "Docker Hub rate-limits ==anonymous== pulls: log in or use a pull-through cache mirror",
            "`docker login` saves credentials in `config.json`, ideally via a credential helper",
            "Retention and garbage collection policies keep storage cost down"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Pushing images with **baked-in secrets**: every layer is readable by anyone who can pull",
            "Deleting a secret in a later layer does not remove it from earlier layers",
            "Deploying `latest`: the same tag can pull different content"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Interview Point",
          "items": [
            "Why is a repeat push of the same image fast?",
            "What does a manifest list do for multi-arch images?",
            "Why pin by digest instead of by tag?",
            "How do you avoid Docker Hub pull limits?"
          ],
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Key Takeaways",
          "text": "Tag for humans, pin digests for machines, and never ship a secret in any layer."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Push, pull, tag, pin"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Docker Security",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Why Layers Matter",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A container shares the host kernel, so its boundary is ==weaker than a VM==",
            "One control is never enough, so stack several: ==defence in depth==",
            "Run as non-root with `USER`: root in a container is **root on the host** after an escape",
            "Every later control shrinks what a compromised process can do"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Runtime Hardening",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`--cap-drop=ALL`, then add back only what is needed",
            "`--read-only` root filesystem plus `--tmpfs` for writable paths",
            "`--security-opt no-new-privileges` blocks ==setuid== escalation",
            "Default ==seccomp== profile blocks about 44 risky syscalls",
            "AppArmor or SELinux add mandatory access control"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "Process",
                "sub": "syscall"
              },
              {
                "text": "seccomp",
                "sub": "filter calls"
              },
              {
                "text": "Capabilities",
                "sub": "dropped set"
              },
              {
                "text": "AppArmor / SELinux",
                "sub": "MAC policy"
              },
              {
                "text": "Kernel",
                "sub": "allowed only"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Root Mapping Compared",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mode",
            "Container root is",
            "Risk"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Default",
              "host UID 0",
              "escape = root"
            ],
            [
              "userns-remap",
              "unprivileged UID",
              "daemon-wide map"
            ],
            [
              "Rootless",
              "user-owned daemon",
              "no host root"
            ],
            [
              "--privileged",
              "all caps, devices",
              "no isolation"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Supply Chain and Secrets",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Scan for CVEs with ==Docker Scout==, Trivy or Grype in CI",
            "Use minimal or ==distroless== bases and pinned `@sha256` digests",
            "Verify signatures with Docker Content Trust or ==cosign==",
            "Secrets via BuildKit `--mount=type=secret` or runtime secrets, never `ENV`/`ARG`"
          ],
          "style": "check"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Hardened Run",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker run -d --user 1000:1000 \\",
            "  --cap-drop=ALL --read-only \\",
            "  --tmpfs /tmp \\",
            "  --security-opt \\",
            "  no-new-privileges myapp:1.4"
          ],
          "note": "add caps back only if needed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`ENV` or `ARG` secrets show up in **docker history** and `inspect`",
            "Daemon API on unauthenticated TCP ==2375== gives remote root",
            "Using `--privileged` or mounting `/var/run/docker.sock` in app containers",
            "Leaving the image user as root, with every capability kept"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Interview Point",
          "items": [
            "Why is a container less isolated than a VM?",
            "What does `--cap-drop=ALL` change, and what does `no-new-privileges` stop?",
            "Rootless mode vs userns-remap: how do they differ?",
            "Why are `ARG` and `ENV` unsafe for secrets?"
          ],
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Key Takeaways",
          "text": "Run non-root, drop everything, scan and sign images, and keep secrets and the daemon socket out of reach."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Harden the container boundary"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Debugging: State, Logs, Exit Codes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Check State First",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`docker ps -a` lists stopped containers too",
            "`docker inspect c` shows ==ExitCode== and ==OOMKilled==",
            "Same output lists mounts and network settings",
            "Read state before guessing at causes"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Inspect Live Containers",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`docker logs -f --tail 100 --since 10m c` reads stdout and stderr; the logging driver decides storage",
            "`docker exec -it c sh` looks inside a running container",
            "No shell in the image? Use `docker debug` or a sidecar sharing namespaces",
            "`docker stats` and `docker top` show live CPU, memory, processes",
            "`docker events` streams daemon activity: die, oom, health_status"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Exit Codes",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Code",
            "Meaning",
            "Usual cause"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "0",
              "Clean exit",
              "Job finished"
            ],
            [
              "1",
              "App error",
              "Crash, read logs"
            ],
            [
              "125",
              "Daemon error",
              "Bad `docker run` flag"
            ],
            [
              "126",
              "Not executable",
              "Missing exec bit"
            ],
            [
              "127",
              "Command not found",
              "Wrong path in CMD"
            ],
            [
              "137",
              "SIGKILL or OOM",
              "Memory limit hit"
            ],
            [
              "143",
              "SIGTERM",
              "docker stop"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. The Debug Flow",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "Symptom",
              {
                "text": "docker ps -a",
                "sub": "state"
              },
              {
                "text": "inspect + logs",
                "sub": "evidence"
              },
              {
                "text": "exec or sh override",
                "sub": "look inside"
              },
              {
                "text": "Fix Dockerfile",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Symptom Playbook",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Crash loop: restart policy hides it, so read the last attempt's logs",
            "Cannot connect: app binds `0.0.0.0` and the port is published",
            "Containers share a network; `nslookup svc` resolves",
            "Disk full: `docker system df`, then `system prune` and `builder prune`",
            "Build fails: `--progress=plain --no-cache` reveals the step"
          ],
          "style": "check"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker logs --tail 50 web",
            "docker run -it --entrypoint sh app",
            "docker system df",
            "docker build --progress=plain \\",
            "  --no-cache ."
          ],
          "note": "override entrypoint to inspect a crasher"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Key Takeaways",
          "text": "Read state, logs and exit code first, then fix the image, never the running container."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Diagnose before you fix"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Crash Recovery and Cleanup",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Editing a running container: changes are **lost** on recreate",
            "Fix the Dockerfile and rebuild instead",
            "Permission denied on volumes: container UID differs from host file owner",
            "Fix with `chown` on the host path or `--user`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Log Flags",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flag",
            "Effect",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`-f`",
              "Follow live output",
              "`logs -f web`"
            ],
            [
              "`--tail`",
              "Last N lines only",
              "`--tail 100`"
            ],
            [
              "`--since`",
              "Recent time window",
              "`--since 10m`"
            ],
            [
              "`-t`",
              "Add timestamps",
              "`logs -t web`"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Live Evidence",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`docker stats` shows live CPU, memory and network per container",
            "`docker top c` lists the processes inside it",
            "`docker events` streams die, oom and ==health_status==",
            "`inspect -f` pulls one field, such as ==OOMKilled=="
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker stats --no-stream",
            "docker inspect \\",
            "  -f '{{.State.OOMKilled}}' c",
            "docker events \\",
            "  --filter event=oom"
          ],
          "note": "OOMKilled true means raise the limit"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Crash Loop Recovery",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Read the logs of the **previous** attempt first",
            "Run the image with `--entrypoint sh` to look inside",
            "Start the app command by hand and watch the error",
            "Fix the Dockerfile, rebuild, then redeploy"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Disk and Cache Cleanup",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Command",
            "Reclaims"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`docker system df`",
              "Shows usage only"
            ],
            [
              "`docker system prune`",
              "Stopped, dangling"
            ],
            [
              "`docker builder prune`",
              "Build cache"
            ],
            [
              "`docker volume prune`",
              "Unused volumes"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Cannot Connect Checklist",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "App binds `0.0.0.0`, not `127.0.0.1`, inside the container",
            "Port is published: `-p 8080:80` shows in `docker ps`",
            "Both containers share one user-defined network",
            "`nslookup svc` resolves the service name",
            "Published ports bypass ufw rules: check iptables too"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Images Without a Shell",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`docker debug c` attaches a toolbox to a slim image",
            "Or run a sidecar sharing the target's namespaces",
            "`--pid container:c` shares processes; `--network container:c` shares the network",
            "Distroless images ship no `sh`, so `exec` fails"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Prune Carefully",
          "text": "`volume prune` deletes data for good, so check `docker volume ls` first."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Interview Point",
          "items": [
            "What does exit code 137 mean, and how do you confirm OOM?",
            "A container restarts endlessly: how do you find why?",
            "How do you debug an image that has no shell?",
            "Why is editing a running container a bad fix?"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Diagnose before you fix"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Production-Ready Containers and Orchestrators",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Production-Ready Containers",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Containers should be ==stateless==, disposable and configured by **environment**",
            "`HEALTHCHECK` plus a `restart` policy gives self-healing on one host",
            "Set memory and CPU ==limits== and reservations so none starves the host",
            "`--restart unless-stopped` revives crashed or rebooted containers"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Stop Cleanly, Log Safely",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Handle ==SIGTERM== to finish requests, then exit before the grace period ends",
            "`--init` (tini) runs as PID 1 and reaps **zombie** processes",
            "Log to stdout and let a ==logging driver== ship it: json-file, fluentd, gelf",
            "Cap json-file with `max-size` and `max-file`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker run -d --init \\",
            "  --memory 512m --cpus 1 \\",
            "  --restart unless-stopped \\",
            "  --stop-timeout 30 \\",
            "  --log-opt max-size=10m \\",
            "  --log-opt max-file=3 myapp"
          ],
