      "page_title": "Safe Rollouts, Limits and Log Rotation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker build -t app:$SHA .",
            "docker push app:$SHA",
            "docker service update \\",
            "  --image app@sha256:ab12 web",
            "# rollback: redeploy old digest"
          ],
          "note": "Digests are immutable; tags move"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One big container running **many processes**: use one process per container",
            "No log rotation: json-file logs ==fill the disk== until the host stalls",
            "Deploying a mutable tag, so rollback has no exact target"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Safe Rollout Steps",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Build, test and scan the image in CI first",
            "Push it tagged with the ==git SHA==",
            "Update the service to the new **digest**",
            "Watch healthchecks while replicas roll one by one",
            "On failure, redeploy the previous digest"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Swarm vs Kubernetes",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
